  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A CONSERVATION RESEARCH PROGRAM FOR BIRDS OF THE GRAN CHACO</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Habitat loss and fragmentation due to rapid deforestation of the Gran Chaco poses a major threat to Nearctic-Neotropical migratory birds that winter in this ecoregion. This project has four main components: (1) Develop a regional bird survey program to establish the distribution, abundance and critical habitats for 15 Nearctic-Neotropical migratory land birds that winter in the Gran Chaco, which will serve as baseline data for future applied conservation research to identify and mitigate threats impacting their populations; (2) Establish collaborations across academic institutions and conservation organization linked by shared migratory land birds; (3) Develop a research project to understand limiting factors during the nonbreeding season; and (4) Resolve gaps in our understanding of the migratory connectivity of Yellow-billed Cuckoo.</narrative>
  </description>
